---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | The Little AI Company"
  description="The Little AI Company privacy posture for launch measurement and visitor trust."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>
  <section class="page-section privacy-page" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 id="privacy-title">Measured lightly, explained plainly.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        TLAC can learn from launch traffic without turning the site into a
        tracking surface. The default build keeps analytics off.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="privacy-grid">
      <section class="privacy-panel" aria-labelledby="privacy-default-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-default-title">Default measurement setting</h2>
        <p>
          The default website build ships with no analytics beacon, tracking
          script, provider token, cookie write, or localStorage tracking write.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-panel" aria-labelledby="privacy-no-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-no-title">What TLAC does not do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>No ads.</li>
          <li>No retargeting.</li>
          <li>No private personal context.</li>
          <li>No account, contact, or form data collection.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-panel" aria-labelledby="privacy-optional-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-optional-title">Optional launch analytics</h2>
        <p>
          If Jeff approves analytics for launch, the site can enable a small
          Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon at build time. That setting is
          configurable and is not active in the default build.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="privacy-panel" aria-labelledby="privacy-questions-title">
        <h2 id="privacy-questions-title">What measurement is for</h2>
        <p>
          Measurement should answer simple product questions: which public pages
          are useful, which projects need clearer proof, and which routes deserve
          better explanation.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
